<article class="env-lemma" id="0H0B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H0B">Lemma <span data-tag="0H0B">96.24.3</span>.</a> Let $p : \mathcal{X} \to (\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ be a category fibred in groupoids. Let $\tau \in \{ Zariski, {\acute{e}tale}, smooth, syntomic, fppf\} $. The functor $\mathcal{X}_{affine, \tau } \to \mathcal{X}_\tau $ is a special cocontinuous functor. Hence it induces an equivalence of topoi from $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{X}_{affine, \tau })$ to $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{X}_\tau )$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
